.TH CHMAP_RESET 3 "2026-10-31" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chmap_reset \- clear all entries from a hash map (type-inferred wrapper)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

chmap_reset(chm, new_bucket_array_size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for chashmap_reset(). It takes the same arguments
and gives the same result; chashmap_reset(3) has the full contract.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
chm                      Hash map to reset
new_bucket_array_size    Number of buckets after the reset; see
                         chashmap_reset(3)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The code chashmap_reset(3) gives: ccol_success, or
ccol_not_enough_memory when the resize failed and the entries are
cleared anyway.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chashmap_reset (3)
